=== COMPILE-ONLY LOCALLY; RUNTIME ON RENTAL (W5) ===
gfx942 (MI300) is the report headline AMD part, but there is NO MI300 hardware on
this host (local GPU = gfx1101). `hipcc --offload-arch=gfx942` is a target-
independent clang AMDGPU codegen step: it cross-compiles the portable kernels to a
gfx942 code object WITHOUT needing the device. Therefore EVERY MI300 figure below
is "compile-only locally; runtime on rental (W5)". The runtime launch + golden
correctness on real MI300 is deferred to the Wave 5 rental. The matching negative
(attempting to RUN a gfx942 binary locally -> graceful "no gfx942 device,
compile-only", not a crash) is in reports/w4_gfx942_norun.log.

=== PORTABILITY PROOF (unchanged source) ===
The SAME committed kernels/generated/*.cu that compile for gfx1101 (Todo 19) and
that nvcc builds with -DPOLYKERNEL_CUDA cross-compile UNCHANGED for gfx942 under
`hipcc --offload-arch=gfx942 -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP`. Only the --offload-arch flag
changes; the portable source (kernels/template/kernel_common.h, pk_* / PK_* names)
is byte-identical.

=== ISA CAPTURE (reuses the Todo 21 AMD ISA analyzer) ===
hipcc_driver.py --all implies --dump-isa: after each clean compile it reuses
amd_analyze.py (hipcc --save-temps + parse of the emitted .amdhsa metadata) to
read VGPR/SGPR/LDS/scratch/spills from the cross-compiled .s. No GPU of the target
arch is required — the ISA is parsed from the .s, which is exactly how the MI300
figures are obtained without hardware. (The [amd_analyze] lines below are those
--save-temps compiles.) Occupancy / runtime metrics are NOT claimed for gfx942
here — they need the real device (W5 rental).

=== COMMAND ===
nix develop --impure --accept-flake-config -c \
  python3 tools/polykernel-bench/hipcc_driver.py --arch gfx942 --all

